[0m
[32m| **Eligibility** | Non‑profit, academic, or for‑profit entities worldwide that **develop, expand, or align a global real‑world data platform** for AD/ADRD. Must not have an “Incomplete” AA award or overlapping AA grant. |
[0m
[32m| **Fit for AHA** | – Directly targets **real‑world data platforms** with **international reach** (criterion a). <br>– Requires **patient/physician registry or cohort study** (criterion c) – AHA Connect will host a registry‑style cohort. <br>– Budget request of US $350 k fits comfortably within the award range. |
[0m
[32m| **Red Flags** | – The AA prohibits **salary or financial benefit** to members of the Medical & Scientific Advisory Group (MSAG) or International Research Grant Program (IRGP) Council; AHA must ensure no such individuals receive compensation. <br>– Must submit a **pre‑submission inquiry** before full application (rolling). |
[0m
[32m| **Supporting Quote** | “ALZ‑RWD awards range from $100,000 to $1,000,000 for 12–24 month projects… the next deadline for full applications is **June 30 2027**.” ([GrantAnchor, 2026](https://grantanchor.com/grant/GA-03023/alzheimers-association-global-real-world-data-programs-funding-alz-rwd)) |

[0m
[32m**Why it is a priority:** This is the **largest single source of non‑dilutive funding** explicitly earmarked for AD real‑world data platforms, and it explicitly values **health‑equity** and **global reach**, both central to AHA’s mission.

